        <article>
          <h1>Feeds &amp; sitemap</h1>
          <p>With a canonical <code>url</code> set, Baudelaire emits a <code>sitemap.xml</code> of every page plus RSS and/or Atom feeds of your most recent dated pages.</p>
          <pre><code data-lang="kdl"><span style="color: #e5d005">url</span> <span style="color: #e5d008">"</span><span style="color: #e5d002">https://example.com</span><span style="color: #e5d008">"</span>

<span style="color: #e5d005">output</span> <span style="color: #e5d008">{</span>
  <span style="color: #e5d005">feed</span> <span style="color: #e5d008">{</span>
    <span style="color: #e5d005">formats</span> <span style="color: #e5d008">"</span><span style="color: #e5d002">rss</span><span style="color: #e5d008">"</span> <span style="color: #e5d008">"</span><span style="color: #e5d002">atom</span><span style="color: #e5d008">"</span>
    <span style="color: #e5d005">limit</span> <span style="color: #e5d003">20</span>
  <span style="color: #e5d008">}</span>
<span style="color: #e5d008">}</span></code></pre>
          <p>A page joins the feed when its frontmatter has a <code>date</code>; <code>limit</code> caps how many of the newest appear. The footer of this site links its <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>, <a href="/atom.xml">Atom</a>, and <a href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap</a>.</p>
          <div class="callout callout-note">
            <p class="callout-label">NOTE</p>
            Feeds and the sitemap need absolute links, so they only emit when <code>url</code> is set. On a preview host, pass <code>--base-url</code> to point them at the right origin.
          </div>
